From a8540100968956b5b5c6b7a9d18d4952f3c472b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Edley <1334816+brandonedley@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 19:04:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Add opt-in -wex-s0-csb-resync for S0ix Deep Idle wake

Add an opt-in -wex-s0-csb-resync boot argument to preserve retained
Tiger Lake / Alder Lake execlist CSB state across S0ix Deep Idle wakes
without requiring an external GT reset:

- No-reset CSB preservation and resync (adapted from #80 by 91270 and
  rodgod-rr): qualify and hook IntelAccelerator::systemWillSleep and
  systemDidWake, snapshot drained CSB state (CSB_PTR, HWS tail,
  software head, GFX_MODE, active execlist bank, EXECLIST_STATUS, and
  slot pointers) on sleep, drop spurious mid-sleep CSB interrupts, and
  preserve matching retained state on resetOnWake instead of resetting
  CSB_PTR and poisoning HWSP. Fall back to re-arming GFX_MODE bit 3 (if
  lost, including on never-initialized engines after an early GPU reset)
  and normal TGLCSB::initialize() otherwise.
- Opt-in same-context ElementComplete handling (adapted from #171 c4 by
  jkbuha): classifyS0()/legacyEntryS0() handle away == to with
  newQueue == 0 and detail == 0 while leaving default classify() and
  legacyEntry() unchanged.
- Boot-only wrapTGLAcceleratorEngine checks under -wex-s0-csb-resync:
  gate the ADL-N/ADL-P GGTT walk and diagnostic setProperty block on
  tglHost.startingOwner == that so post-boot wakes do not re-run them.
- Register -wex-s0-csb-resync in tests/fixtures/boot_argument_names.json
  and add CPU unit tests in tests/tgl_csb.cpp covering wake planning,
  never-initialized engine mode re-arm, readTail, and same-context
  ElementComplete handling.

Without -wex-s0-csb-resync, runtime behavior is unchanged.
